From: nuno407 <11352538+nuno407@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:30:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/45] ARM: dts: tegra30: surface-rt: route the headphone
 outputs to the jack-switched pin

The machine driver toggles the DAPM pins "Headphone" and "Headphones" from
the hp-det GPIO, but the routing used the "Headphone Jack" widget, which no
jack controls. The headphone path was therefore always powered with the
DAC and the "Headphones Switch" control did nothing. Route HPOUTL/R to
"Headphones" so the jack powers the headphone driver up and down.
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
index c8ec47ae1..2f7a62306 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
@@ -819,8 +819,8 @@ sound {
 		nvidia,model = "Microsoft Surface RT WM8962";
 
 		nvidia,audio-routing =
-			"Headphone Jack", "HPOUTR",
-			"Headphone Jack", "HPOUTL",
+			"Headphones", "HPOUTR",
+			"Headphones", "HPOUTL",
 			"Int Spk", "SPKOUTR",
 			"Int Spk", "SPKOUTL",
 			"DMICDAT", "Int Mic";
-- 
2.47.3

